# Raw source files - preserve verbatim bytes across platforms. Ofcom (and
# other data sources we'll mirror later) serve CSVs / PDFs / XLSX etc. with
# source-specific bytes; without this marker, git's default text
# normalisation would alter CRLF-terminated CSVs on Windows commit, so the
# LXC checkout would have different bytes than the live download - breaking
# the archive idempotence check that hashes staging CSVs against archived
# raw.csv hashes.
archive/**/raw.*           binary
latest-raw.*               binary
amateur-callsigns-raw.csv  binary

# Derived normalised.csv must be byte-stable across platforms (meta.json
# records its sha256/size and the sweep no-op check is byte equality) while
# staying diffable text - pin LF, never smudge to CRLF on checkout.
archive/**/normalised.csv text eol=lf
# stats.json and quality reports: byte-compared derivatives like normalised.csv
# - pin LF so Windows checkouts cannot break no-op detection or meta hashes.
archive/**/stats.json  text eol=lf
archive/**/components.csv  text eol=lf
reports/**  text eol=lf
